From 310b22025089dbdd6c2f5a0606ae4aed61fe6867 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Oskari=20Lemmel=C3=A4?= <oskari@lemmela.net>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 21:26:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] net: pse-pd: add MikroTik RouterBOARD PoE PSE controller
 driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add support for the SPI-connected PoE controller on the MikroTik
RB960PGS (hEX PoE), allowing its four PoE output ports to be controlled
and monitored through the standard ethtool PSE interface. The board is
QCA9557-based (ath79) and uses the native SPI controller handled by
spi-ar934x.

The controller uses a CRC8-protected command protocol. Integrate it with
the Clause 33 PSE framework to expose port enable/disable, administrative
and power status, extended fault information and actual delivered power.
Provide supply-voltage readings through the PSE regulator interface.
Expose pse-pis nodes referenced by Ethernet PHYs through the pses
property.

Use administrative-mode encodings checked in MCU firmware 6.49.20,
7.20.7 and 7.23.2. The analyzed 7.x images translate command modes
0/1/2 to 0x00/0x01/0x22 and publish the low nibble for each port,
preserving disabled/forced/automatic readbacks. Extract the mode from
peek replies, whose high byte echoes the index, and reject unrecognized
mode nibbles rather than interpreting an unknown mode as disabled.

The board supports passive PoE at lower supply voltages as well as
802.3af/at output with a suitable supply. Register the controller
independently of supply voltage so PHY registration does not depend on
an af/at-capable supply, and leave voltage limits to the firmware.

Attempt an explicit power-off recovery when an enable command fails,
since firmware may have accepted it before reply validation failed.
The core retains uncertainty so a subsequent disable can retry.

Provide a debugfs force_mode control for passive power output without PD
detection or classification. Document that it affects subsequent hardware
enables, not already-enabled ports or current per-port mode. Read-only
state and peek entries expose raw MCU status to help diagnose slow or
failing PD detection.

Signed-off-by: Oskari Lemmelä <oskari@lemmela.net>
