 .../networking/pse-pd/introduction.rst        |  23 +
 drivers/net/pse-pd/Kconfig                    |  15 +
 drivers/net/pse-pd/Makefile                   |   1 +
 drivers/net/pse-pd/mikrotik_poe.c             | 935 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 974 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/net/pse-pd/mikrotik_poe.c

--- a/Documentation/networking/pse-pd/introduction.rst
+++ b/Documentation/networking/pse-pd/introduction.rst
@@ -71,3 +71,26 @@ Physical Layers. In this clause, 'PSE' r
 'PD' to PoDL PD. The key intent is to provide devices with a unified interface
 for both data and the power required to process this data over a single
 balanced twisted-pair Ethernet connection.
+
+MikroTik RouterBOARD diagnostics
+-------------------------------
+
+The ``mikrotik_poe`` driver supports only RB960PGS boards, based on the
+QCA9557 (ath79) platform. The supported board uses the native
+AR934x/QCA95xx SPI controller with the ``spi-ar934x`` driver
+(``CONFIG_SPI_AR934X``).
+
+The driver exposes ``force_mode``, ``state`` and ``peek`` in its per-device
+debugfs directory. ``force_mode`` is a controller-wide policy for subsequent
+hardware enables, not a report of each port's current mode. Changing it
+does not reprogram already-enabled ports. Each affected port needs a
+successful disable followed by enable through ethtool for the new policy
+to take effect. Forced mode bypasses PD detection and classification;
+use it only with equipment that accepts the board's passive PoE supply.
+
+Administrative mode encodings were checked by static analysis of MCU
+firmware 6.49.20, 7.20.7 and 7.23.2. In both analyzed 7.x images,
+disabled/forced/automatic commands (0/1/2) translate to 0x00/0x01/0x22,
+whose low nibble is stored for the port. Administrative readback therefore
+preserves 0/1/2. Other administrative modes are reported as protocol
+errors, which can also prevent registration of a PHY referencing this PSE.
